# PYTHON VIRTUALENVS, BY GLOB AND NOT BY NAME — AND THE GLOB IS A DAY 68 FIX.
#
# This file listed `.pe/` and `.venv/` exactly, and `tools/differential/README.md`
# told the next run to put its SECOND policyengine install in `.pe2` — a name
# neither rule covered. Day 67 followed its own advice and committed 74,784 files
# and 838 MB of an AGPL-licensed virtualenv to an MIT repository. See
# NOTES-FOR-HUMAN.md.
#
#   AN IGNORE RULE THAT NAMES A DIRECTORY GUARDS THAT DIRECTORY AND NOTHING THAT
#   RHYMES WITH IT. The README's own warning about `git add -A` over an unignored
#   venv is in the same code block as the suggestion that created one.
#
# `tools/cross-package/tracked-paths.mjs --check` is the guard that does not
# depend on this file being right.
.pe*/
.venv*/
venv/
pyvenv.cfg
__pycache__/
*.pyc
